0,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":-1.673924693273163,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":true,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":100.0,"_gate_accruals":-0.008529378699526363,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":17.2,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.10576451403812917,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":84.1,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.0024091929717325877,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":7,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":77.8,"_gate_spread":0.10129844133984137,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":50.6,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.23453883160818553,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":60.9,"_gate_incr_roic":0.21427054021118883,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":88.1,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.2894659511479338,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":100.0,"_gate_pool_share":0.1440180705954064,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":97.6,"_gate_rev_durability":0.15489412511204148,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.16850948894019702,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":-0.0066345203856103315,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":43.4,"_gate_fund_growth":0.1931261441000432,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":100.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.014348826647950426,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":27.1,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.006284821168119459,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":57.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.07831331286575854,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00524,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":["paper"],"description_full":"Intuitive Surgical, Inc. develops, manufactures, and markets products that enable physicians and healthcare providers to enhance the quality of and access to minimally invasive care in the United States and internationally. It offers the da Vinci Surgical System that enables surgical procedures using a minimally invasive approach; and Ion endoluminal system, which extends its commercial offerings beyond surgery into diagnostic endoluminal procedures enabling minimally invasive biopsies in the lung. The company also provides a suite of stapling, energy, and core instrumentation for its multi-port da Vinci surgical systems; progressive learning pathways to support the use of its technology; infrastructure of customer service and support specialists, a complement of services to its customers, including installation, repair, maintenance, 24/7 technical support, and proactive system health monitoring; and integrated digital capabilities providing connected offerings, streamlining performance for hospitals with program-enhancing insights. It sells its products through direct sales organizations, such as capital and clinical sales teams. Intuitive Surgical, Inc. was incorporated in 1995 and is headquartered in Sunnyvale, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David J. Rosa | CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 17K people. Revenue per employee of $591K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, improving at 15%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $146K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $46K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Intuitive Surgical, Inc. is a large-cap healthcare business with a $160.0B market cap on $10.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +17% over the past three years and +15% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 21% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 10-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 69% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $2.5B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 25 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.06\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 1.4%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 3.3\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 295% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.945924584088545},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $11.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 19% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 29% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Healthcare peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Financial quality scores above most Healthcare peers","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Intuitive Surgical (ISRG) Moved, What Is Catching Investors\u2019 Attention?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nasdaq-isrg/intuitive-surgical/news/intuitive-surgical-isrg-moved-what-is-catching-investors-att","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793985643.878,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.917,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Intuitive Surgical, Inc. (ISRG) is Attracting Investor Attention: Here is What You Should Know","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025342/intuitive-surgical-inc-isrg-is-attracting-investor-attention-here-is-what-you-should-know?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cmost_searched_stocks_v1-3025342","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793970003.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.477,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Can Intuitive Surgical (NASDAQ:ISRG) Move Past Its Legal Overhang?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/healthcare/can-intuitive-surgical-nasdaqisrg-move-past-its-legal-overhang","date":"2026-11-05","timesta